{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nCites re-measured on origin/main `39821ae000a` after `e123` landed; `[0.14.0]` was cut 2026-10-30.\n\n`gen_env_registry.render()` (`scripts/gen_env_registry.py:400`) unions derived names only for `REBAR_MCP_*` (`MCP_ENV_VARS`, `:406-409`), so most settable `REBAR_<SECTION>_<KEY>` names never reach `docs/env-vars.md`. **Do not hardcode the counts.** Measured on `39821ae000a`: 105 canonical names, 65 undocumented — figures every sibling moves. Re-derive before implementing; let the test compute them.\n\nThe canary keeps a \"one-release\" rollback source (`canary_bridge.py:140-143,687`; `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml:28,34,54,134`) two releases after ADR 0094.\n\n**CHANGELOG — the premise changed.** `git merge-base --is-ancestor` shows both commits this story files shipped in **v0.14.0**, and in neither v0.13.0 nor v0.13.1: `334ee94` \"Remove scheduled public deprecations\" and `81da792` \"Retire the HLC rollback switch\" (both 2026-09-03). They do **not** belong in `[Unreleased]` — that was right only before `[0.14.0]` was cut. `334ee94`'s two bullets are misfiled under `[0.13.0]` (`:277-521`) at `:508-515` (the `force=`/`force_close` normalization) and `:517-521` (the `openai-chat` fallback); both move to `[0.14.0]` (`:32`) `### Changed` (`:34`). `81da792` has no entry (`grep REBAR_HLC CHANGELOG.md` is empty) and needs one there. `[Unreleased]` (`:11`) is NOT empty — `cb2b` already filed a bullet under its `### Changed` (`:13`); append, do not create.\n\n## Approach\n- **Registry (decision: derive all).** In `render()` replace the `MCP_ENV_VARS`-only union (`:406-409`) with a loop over `_SECTIONS` calling `_canonical_env_name(sect, key)`, attributing each to `src/rebar/_config_sections.py (canonical env name of {sect}.{key})`; keep the `MCP_ENV_VARS` union for `REBAR_MCP_DEDUP` (in `MCP_ENV_VARS`, not a config key). `_canonical_env_name` is at `src/rebar/_config_sources.py:317`; `_SECTIONS` is importable from `rebar._config_schema` (precedent: `scripts/generate_config_surface_golden.py:48`). Regenerate `docs/env-vars.md`. Do **not** change `scripts/_mechanism_delta/detect_config.py`: `detect_env_vars` (`:83-97`) consumes `registry.scan()` plus its own `_derived_env_names` (`:41-59`), never `render()`, so a `render()`-only edit adds **zero** entries to the mechanism census. No docstring or `docs/architecture.md` edit is needed; the detector's behaviour and its census output are unchanged. Tests: `tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py` add `test_every_canonical_env_name_is_documented` — derive the set from `_SECTIONS`, assert each appears as a ``| `NAME` |`` row, assert **no literal count**. `:43-56` unchanged (`REBAR_PUSH` still absent). `tests/unit/test_env_registry_helper_coverage.py` needs no edit (`_llm_*` helpers only).\n- **Canary.** `scripts/canary_bridge.py`: delete `:140-143` and `:687`; `cmd_check_heartbeat` calls `_check_status_heartbeat` directly; keep `_check_github_heartbeat` (`:255`) for the `NEVER_RUN` bootstrap (call site `:187-196`; ADR 0094 `:81-82` forbids dropping it), make `bootstrap` (`:261`) a required keyword and drop the `if bootstrap` ternary at `:329`. Workflow: delete the `status_source` dispatch input (`:28` description, `:34` choice) and the `REBAR_CANARY_HEARTBEAT_SOURCE` job env (`:54`); `:134` becomes `python scripts/canary_bridge.py check-heartbeat`. The named `run:` steps censused as `ci_gate::` rows in `.github/mechanism-baseline.json:299-310` stay; `REBAR_CANARY_HEARTBEAT_SOURCE` has no `env_var::` row, so the mechanism ratchet is unaffected. Docs: `docs/jira-sync-setup.md:191` (delete sentence), `:294` (delete row); `docs/adr/0094-reconciler-last-pass-two-witness-status.md` append a dated \"Status\" paragraph after `:82`.\n- **Canary tests — the file set AC2's grep compels.** `tests/scripts/test_canary_bridge.py:71` remove the key and have `hb_env`'s runner answer `rebar bridge status` with `{\"verdict\":\"NEVER_RUN\"}` so the run-history math is exercised via bootstrap. `tests/scripts/test_canary_bridge_heldout.py`: `:74`, **`:122`**, `:145`, and delete the rollback test covering `:168`. `:122` sets the key to `\"status\"`, not `\"github-api\"`, which is why earlier passes missed it. `tests/scripts/test_canary_status_refs_heldout.py:133` remove the key.\n- **CHANGELOG.** Move `:508-515` and `:517-521` out of `[0.13.0]` into `[0.14.0]` `### Changed` (`:34`). Add under `[0.14.0]`: \"- **BREAKING (pre-1.0): the `REBAR_HLC=0` rollback switch is removed.** The HLC is always on; the variable is ignored (commit `81da792`, ticket `fdd1-12fa-ce83-45d1`).\" Leave `:639` (historical cross-reference) and `:1361` (the 2025 entry recording `force_close`'s introduction) where they are. Append to `[Unreleased]`'s existing `### Changed` (`:13`) only this epic's remaining unreleased work: the alias-tombstone entry, the `[llm]` unknown-key entry, the test-hooks entry (\"test-only `REBAR_HLC_NOW` / `REBAR_TEST_COMPACT_RENAME_BARRIER` are no longer read by rebar\"), and \"`docs/env-vars.md` now lists every `REBAR_<SECTION>_<KEY>` override\". Mirror in `docs/release-notes.md`.\n\n## Scope\n`scripts/gen_env_registry.py`, `docs/env-vars.md`, `tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py`, `scripts/canary_bridge.py`, `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml`, `docs/jira-sync-setup.md`, `docs/adr/0094-reconciler-last-pass-two-witness-status.md`, `tests/scripts/test_canary_bridge.py`, `tests/scripts/test_canary_bridge_heldout.py`, `tests/scripts/test_canary_status_refs_heldout.py`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/release-notes.md`. Out of scope: `detect_config.py:63-81` detector logic, `.github/mechanism-baseline.json`, `tests/unit/test_env_registry_helper_coverage.py`, the `_check_github_heartbeat` bootstrap path (ADR 0094 `:81-82`), `scripts/_mechanism_delta/detect_config.py`, `docs/architecture.md`, and the historical `docs/release-notes.md:1411-1413` (the v0.14.0 record, deliberately retained; the new `[Unreleased]` entry records the retirement) and `CHANGELOG.md:639,1361`.\n\n## Testing\n- `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py --check` clean after regeneration; spot-check `grep -n 'REBAR_VERIFY_REQUIRE_PLAN_REVIEW_FOR_CLAIM\\|REBAR_COMPACTION_HORIZON_NS' docs/env-vars.md` both present. Do not assert a row total.\n- `pytest tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py tests/scripts/test_canary_bridge*.py tests/scripts/test_canary_status_refs_heldout.py tests/unit/test_canary_bridge_wiring.py tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py -q`.\n- Edge, by hand and **not** committed (the literals break AC2's grep): `check-heartbeat --source status` -> argparse error (exit 2, flag gone); the env var set -> ignored. Committed instead: a `NEVER_RUN` fake still yields the bootstrap witness, output containing `(last-pass producer bootstrap fallback)`.\n- `make verify`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] AC1 Every name produced by `_SECTIONS` x `_canonical_env_name` appears as a row in `docs/env-vars.md`, asserted by the new `test_every_canonical_env_name_is_documented` deriving both sides; `gen_env_registry.py --check` clean. No literal count appears in the AC, the test, or Testing — upstream siblings move every figure.\n- [ ] AC2 `git grep -n 'REBAR_CANARY_HEARTBEAT_SOURCE\\|github-api' -- scripts .github tests` is **empty**; `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` green. Pre-state to confirm before implementing: **14 hits** across 5 files, all in scope (the grep does not over-match). `test_canary_bridge_heldout.py:122` is one of them. (BRE alternation is deliberate: `git grep -E` ignores `\\b`, so an `-E` rewrite can match nothing and pass vacuously.)\n- [ ] AC3 `CHANGELOG.md` `[0.13.0]` no longer contains the `force=`/`force_close` or `openai-chat` bullets; `[0.14.0]` carries both plus a `REBAR_HLC` entry; `[Unreleased]` carries this epic's four entries. Verified by asserting each bullet's section membership, not a line-number threshold — `:639` and `:1361` are historical and must not move.\n- [ ] AC4 `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0; `make verify` green."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793458539051637001,"uuid":"32cda1cb-1f4c-4d88-bf5d-aeb3e87a6b02"}